{
  "name": "402. ElevenLabs speech, transcription and sound effects meet the contract (elevenlabs contract)",
  "description": "TXE-6524, contract C4, C5, C6 and C10 on the built-in elevenlabs provider, with the headers Tokun sends (x-bf-api-key naming one key, x-bf-passthrough-extra-params). Speech: voice_settings carries only the settings the caller gave (before, a request with only speed also sent stability 0, similarity_boost 0, style 0 and use_speaker_boost false, replacing the vendor's defaults); the credits of ElevenLabs' character-cost response header are usage.vendor_cost {amount, unit: credit}, in the x-bifrost-usage header of a byte response and on the speech.audio.done frame of an SSE one, while the header itself is still forwarded; the byte response is labeled with the format asked for (the shared writer of TXE-6530, proved here for mp3, opus and pcm). Transcription: usage is {type: duration, seconds} equal to ElevenLabs' audio_duration_secs; a form field Bifrost does not map (keyterms, transcript_edit, detect_speaker_roles) is written to the form sent upstream, which case 402.6 observes by sending a keyterm ElevenLabs refuses for its length (before, the field was dropped and the request returned 200); a vendor error keeps the vendor's status and carries error_type. Sound effects: an out-of-range duration_seconds or prompt_influence is 400 caller_unsupported_parameter naming the field, with no upstream call (before, 40 was clamped to 30 and 1.5 to 1), and usage no longer reports the requested duration as audio_seconds. Not reproducible against the live vendor, and pinned elsewhere: a 200 with no audio returning 502 provider_empty_result with the vendor's headers is case 330.6 on the provider error fixture (the handler is the same for every provider) and the Go tests TestWriteSpeechAudioElevenlabsEmptyAudioKeepsCharacterCost and TestElevenlabsTranscriptionEmptyAnswerIsProviderEmptyResult; the multichannel duration is TestTranscriptionUsageIsTheVendorAudioDuration.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "402.1 elevenlabs/eleven_turbo_v2_5 - byte speech with only speed: audio/mpeg, character-cost forwarded and reported as vendor_cost, one call on the pinned key (elevenlabs contract)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-api-key",
            "value": "ElevenLabs API Key"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-passthrough-extra-params",
            "value": "true"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"elevenlabs/eleven_turbo_v2_5\",\n  \"input\": \"Hello from the contract harness.\",\n  \"voice\": \"21m00Tcm4TlvDq8ikWAM\",\n  \"speed\": 1.1\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/audio/speech",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "audio",
            "speech"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('mp3 (the default) audio comes back labeled audio/mpeg', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.eql(200);",
              "  var ct = (pm.response.headers.get('content-type') || '').split(';')[0].trim();",
              "  pm.expect(ct).to.eql('audio/mpeg');",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.responseSize, 'audio bytes').to.be.above(0);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('character-cost is forwarded and x-bifrost-usage carries it as vendor_cost in credits', function () {",
              "  var cost = pm.response.headers.get('character-cost');",
              "  pm.expect(cost, 'ElevenLabs sent no character-cost header').to.be.a('string').and.to.match(/^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$/);",
              "  var u = JSON.parse(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-usage') || 'null');",
              "  pm.expect(u, 'no x-bifrost-usage header').to.be.an('object');",
              "  pm.expect(u.vendor_cost, JSON.stringify(u)).to.eql({ amount: Number(cost), unit: 'credit' });",
              "  pm.expect(u, 'a request value or Bifrost count reported as the vendor\\'s').to.not.have.any.keys('audio_seconds', 'billed_characters');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('served by the pinned key, no fallback: one upstream call', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-routing-info-key'), 'routing key').to.eql('ElevenLabs API Key');",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-routing-info-is-fallback') || 'false').to.eql('false');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
